  "description": "Variation of condition 1 and removal of condition 5 of planning permission dated 1st October 2024 (RN 24/03863/FULL) for the Variation of condition 1 of planning permission dated 15 April 2024 (RN: 23/08592/FULL) for the: External refurbishment and works of alteration comprising the replacement of upper floor windows, refurbishment and re-configuration of ground floor shopfronts onto New Bond Street, Brook Street, installation of partially openable shopfront facing Horse Shoe Yard, creation of a new entrance at the corner of New Bond Street and Brook Street, installation of new shopfront doors to replace existing chrome gates fronting New Bond Street and replacement and installation of new rooftop plant. (SITE INCLUDES 111-117 New Bond Street). Namely, the addition of new entrance doors to the proposed office space facing Lancashire Court; removal of the curved corner retail door and replacement with an inward-opening flush glass door in the adjacent bay fronting New Bond Street (unit 1); reduce area of L5 slab demolition and alter the arrangement of mechanical plant equipment and vertical extension of L5 service lift. (Application under S73)",
